TI  - Linker-Mediated Inactivation of the SAM-II Domain in the Tandem SAM-II/SAM-V 
      Riboswitch.
LID - 10.3390/ijms252011288 [doi]
LID - 11288
AB  - Tandem SAM-II/SAM-V riboswitch belongs to a class of riboswitches found in the 
      marine bacterium 'Candidatus Pelagibacter ubique'. Previous studies have 
      demonstrated that these riboswitches have the potential for digital modulation of 
      gene expression at both the transcriptional and translational levels. In this 
      study, we investigate the conformational changes in the tandem SAM-II/SAM-V 
      riboswitch binding to S-adenosylmethionine (SAM) using selective 2'-hydroxyl 
      acylation analyzed by the primer extension (SHAPE) assay, small-angle X-ray 
      scattering (SAXS), and oligos depressing probing. Our findings reveal that the 
      linker between SAM-II/SAM-V aptamers blocks the SAM response of the SAM-II 
      domain. This result proposes a new mechanism for gene expression regulation, 
      where the ligand-binding functions of tandem riboswitches can be selectively 
      masked or released through a linker.
